        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.652,
            0.307,
            0.674
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Figure it Out"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.158,
            0.685,
            0.828,
            0.728
          ],
          "content": "1. What radius should be taken in the compass to get this half circle? What should be the length of AX?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.159,
            0.733,
            0.828,
            0.776
          ],
          "content": "2. Take a central line of a different length and try to draw the wave on it."
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "bbox": [
            0.449,
            0.97,
            0.55,
            0.985
          ],
          "content": "Reprint 2026-27"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.16,
            0.781,
            0.791,
            0.867
          ],
          "content": "3. Try to recreate the figure where the waves are smaller than a half circle (as appearing in the neck of the figure, ‘A Person’). The challenge here is to get both the waves to be identical. This may be tricky!"
